                "text": "**Defining the Color Scheme**\n\nI've established that the divider color is designated as 9. I've also defined the template in position (0,0). I've got the following template: 00000, 04440, 04040, 04440, 00000, which functions as an 8-cell hollow square. I've now identified this pattern: (1,1), (1,2), (1,3), (2,1), (2,3), (3,1), (3,2), (3,3). This is relative to the block's top-left corner at (0,0).\n\n\n**Refining the Block Logic**\n\nI've determined the rule for populating each block: cells in the hollow square template will become 4 or 9 based on their initial value. The center and border cells remain untouched, and the divider lines stay empty. This creates the visual effect by correctly rendering the cells which should contain the required values. I've double checked the logic against several test cases and confirmed it works.\n\n\n",
